          "pdf_to": 127,
          "note": "Acid hydrolysis of nitriles: a main subheading of 24.4 Alkanenitriles, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 127-127."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "When a nitrile is heated with a dilute acid, such as dilute hydrochloric acid or dilute sulphuric acid, a carboxylic acid is formed."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\underset{\\text{ethanenitrile}}{\\ce{CH3CN_{(aq)}}} + \\ce{2H2O_{(l)} + HCl_{(aq)} ->} \\underset{\\text{ethanoic acid}}{\\ce{CH3COOH_{(aq)}}} + \\ce{NH4Cl_{(aq)}}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃CN(aq) (ethanenitrile) + 2H₂O(l) + HCl(aq) → CH₃COOH(aq) (ethanoic acid) + NH₄Cl(aq)"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
